Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Null hypothesis versus RHUFT hypothesis", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0efa85ac-4783-1541-bdd3-e930125086b1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3.1. Null hypothesis", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6e522171-a7bf-1748-9d80-e69ea5b22326"],

Cell["\<\
For matched calibration conditions, differences between instrument geometries \
are fully accounted for by known transfer functions, noise, and boundary \
conditions. No additional closure-sensitive or scale-history-sensitive \
observability effects exist. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1bcb95ac-a209-064c-8ffb-5c9ebebc0fca"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3.2. RHUFT-style alternative", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5755f6c6-2b2d-914e-a665-7f86f31916ce"],

Cell["\<\
For matched calibration conditions, some instrument geometries produce \
systematically different stabilized observables or predictive residual \
structure that is not fully explained by standard reduced transfer models and \
is better captured by enriched geometry-scale-history measurement-state \
descriptors.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"50bb585f-b09d-e64f-a8b2-cec28c92de97"],

Cell["This is a strong but testable claim. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b447815-7405-7146-926e-55ed62e5469c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     TemplateBox[{0},
      "Spacer1"]},
    {
     TemplateBox[{0},
      "Spacer1"]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   FrameStyle->Directive[
     LightDarkSwitched[
      GrayLevel[0.8], 
      GrayLevel[0.4867756]], 
     AbsoluteThickness[1]],
   GridBoxDividers->{
    "Columns" -> {False, {True}, False}, "Rows" -> {False, {True}, False}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Fit}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Text", "MarkdownDelimiter",
 ShowStringCharacters->False,
 Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"9708565a-fea2-2d4c-9098-90b4ede5b676"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. First operational prediction class", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6b2b3a35-3efe-f446-8d50-3e68a8bf6d81"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4.1. Prediction P1: geometry-sensitive residual compression", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bfb80a09-e1e2-684f-86b8-486ea827437d"],

Cell["\<\
If an enriched measurement-state vector is used instead of a scalar output \
only, prediction residuals across repeated trials should reduce for at least \
some sensor classes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04871c24-a6a2-2446-be58-3f5ebf5c73bb"],

Cell["This is realistic and measurable. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b6c43d08-504f-3645-bbcf-0044f296fc21"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
4.2. Prediction P2: recurrence-sensitive hysteresis structure\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b6d7c73b-d36e-b646-8f93-2d34bbf433a2"],

Cell["\<\
Sensors with strong recurrence geometry such as loops, toroidal channels, or \
re-entrant cavities may exhibit reproducible path-dependent response classes \
not well captured by simple scalar calibration curves. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42e5e917-775e-d34e-9a25-73f4558a94df"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4.3. Prediction P3: multiscale observability banding", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9fdd2d46-f3f2-524f-9943-2653ca843bb4"],

Cell["\<\
As resolution or probing bandwidth changes, some features should appear only \
within particular geometry-scale coupling windows rather than monotonically \
improving with finer measurement.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6770866c-71bd-004f-97c9-497781e7fa28"],

Cell["\<\
This would support the claim that observability is band-structured rather \
than simply improved by finer access. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8938c4fc-70dc-184a-b483-afd68132942f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
4.4. Prediction P4: golden-angle or irrational spacing layouts may reduce \
aliasing or mode crowding\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5ff7fb30-c75b-d148-a320-7c4068bc56af"],

Cell["\<\
This must be treated carefully. The prediction is not mystical. It is: \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e06d2982-5b4d-c841-a6a7-535a31602b97"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {
    PaneBox["\<\"sensor arrays using irrational angular spacing may suppress \
coherent degeneracies and sampling artifacts better than certain regular \
layouts.\"\>",
     BaseStyle->{"Text", FontColor -> LightDarkSwitched[
         GrayLevel[0.35], 
         GrayLevel[0.8602474]]},
     ImageMargins->5,
     ImageSize->{Full, Automatic}]}
  },
  AutoDelete->False,
  GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{
       LightDarkSwitched[
        GrayLevel[1], 
        GrayLevel[0.278317]]}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"ColumnsIndexed" -> {1 -> Directive[
        LightDarkSwitched[
         RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1], 
         RGBColor[0.2491127, 0.3295188, 0.4231198]], 
        AbsoluteThickness[4]]}, "Rows" -> {{False}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{
   "Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}]], "Text", \
"BlockQuote",
 Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"28bd7d8e-650d-5d4c-9d15-c272165c7758"],

Cell["\<\
This is very plausible and testable in signal processing and antenna \
arrangements. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"467788d5-681c-c248-b9d5-54385ffe32a3"],

