Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["18. A falsification-centered summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c842fa64-8df5-154d-a0e8-0656901c2598"],

Cell["\<\
The framework gains scientific standing only if one or more of the following \
happens: \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8c80a4ce-d20f-354f-8372-109371215fbb"],

Cell["\<\
enriched measurement-state models predict data better than reduced models,\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fa8359b1-dda4-ab4c-921c-7e9fac902a2a"],

Cell["\<\
geometry-controlled experiments reveal stable residual structure that \
standard models miss,\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0e468f84-eb73-684c-8ab5-bb9732b43dd6"],

Cell["recurrence-aware calibration yields reproducible gains,", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8f6aa8bd-28b5-2940-8f3e-802e04ea6524"],

Cell["\<\
multiscale observability windows appear as real empirical structure.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c914788b-76a4-9749-b2f8-7772766a218d"],

Cell["\<\
If none of these happen, then the RHUFT measurement theory should be weakened \
or rejected.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"053baac0-a10c-7648-8cbb-68e7d00eb768"],

Cell["This is the correct scientific attitude. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8dd55bdd-ad45-bd4c-abe4-8f60416aa8f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     TemplateBox[{0},
      "Spacer1"]},
    {
